# Copy to .env.local (gitignored) for local dev against a real Supabase
# project. Not needed for the GH Pages mock-API build — that path never
# reads these.

# Supabase Dashboard -> Project Settings -> API -> Project URL
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=

# Supabase Dashboard -> Project Settings -> API -> Project API keys -> anon/public
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# --- The following are NOT read from this file. They are Edge Function
# --- secrets, set with `supabase secrets set KEY=value` (see supabase/README.md).

# Stripe Dashboard -> Developers -> API keys -> Secret key (test mode: sk_test_...)
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=

# Stripe Dashboard -> Developers -> Webhooks -> your endpoint -> Signing secret (whsec_...)
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# Supabase Dashboard -> Project Settings -> API -> Project API keys -> service_role
# (server-side only — never expose this in the frontend/browser build)
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Amazon Associates -> Associates Central -> Tools -> CreatorsAPI -> Create App.
# Amazon Creators API (OAuth2 client_credentials) — replaces the old Product
# Advertising API v5 (PA-API v5), which was deprecated April 30, 2026 and
# fully retired May 15, 2026 (every PA-API v5 call now returns a hard 403).
# Old AWS Access/Secret Keys from PA-API do NOT work here — this is a hard
# cutover requiring a new Client ID/Secret. Requires the Associates account
# to have 10+ qualified sales in the trailing 30 days — a rolling window, so
# access can be temporarily revoked if a 30-day period passes with fewer
# than 10 sales, even for a previously-approved account. See
# supabase/README.md for the full writeup and sources.
# AMAZON_CREATORS_CLIENT_ID=
# AMAZON_CREATORS_CLIENT_SECRET=
# AMAZON_CREATORS_PARTNER_TAG=
# Optional overrides (defaults target the India marketplace/standard LWA
# token host — confirm the token host against your Associates Central
# region docs before relying on the default in production):
# AMAZON_CREATORS_TOKEN_URL=https://api.amazon.com/auth/o2/token
# AMAZON_CREATORS_MARKETPLACE=www.amazon.in

# affiliate.flipkart.com -> approved affiliate account
# FLIPKART_AFFILIATE_ID=
# FLIPKART_AFFILIATE_TOKEN=

# Dev/demo ONLY — never set this on a production Supabase project. When
# 'true', search-products returns fake Amazon/Flipkart listings (tagged
# source: 'mock', persisted with a '-mock' suffix) instead of calling the
# real affiliate APIs, so Discover's search box works without any real
# credentials. A real+mock collision on a production project would let demo
# rows silently blend into the real catalog.
# MOCK_MARKETPLACES=true
